ool, consumer path, and the stated behaviour without it, especially memory-capture.sh refusing rather than writing plaintext and runtime_wake NOOP without systemd-run) because a wrong install doc misleads new users\nreview plan: self reads every claim against the cited code; items self (self, anthropic), accuracy (gpt-6.1-sol, openai); budget 12m \u2014 two families checked each claim independently against code, plus two command probes\nran: self: reported in 155s; accuracy: reported in 153s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 no deviation; the what is settled\n\nFindings:\n1. verifiable (self, accuracy): adapters/README.md Adapter map, para 2. The claim \"runtime.py and forge.py share one contract ... exit codes are 0 done, 1 NOOP, 2 refused, 3 could not read\" is false for forge.py. Its CLI exits 1 on ForgeRefusal (scripts/forge.py:617-620). Its NOOP is a typed Python return value (forge.py:131-140, 461), not an exit code. It has no exit 3. Its `auto` reads no markers: it picks gh when gh is on PATH and the ref is numeric (forge.py:596-607). scenario: a caller of the forge.py CLI who follows this doc reads exit 1 as NOOP when it is a refusal. on main: n/a, new text (runtime.py:17 already carries the same claim).\n2. verifiable (self, accuracy): INSTALL.md Dependencies, `gh` row. \"Without it: the none backend\" holds for review but not for landing in a repo that has an origin remote. Probe on a repo with an origin and no gh on PATH: get_forge('auto','12') returns NoneForge, but get_forge('auto','12', landing=True) raises ForgeRefusal \"this repository has an origin remote and gh is not available; landing waits for the forge\" (forge.py:597-600). scenario: a new user cloned from GitHub without gh and expects /merge to land locally; it refuses. on main: n/a.\n3. verifiable (accuracy, self): INSTALL.md `age` row, and README \"the key setup is in INSTALL.md\". The key name is sha256 of the *normalized* origin URL (scheme, user, default port and .git stripped, lowercased), not of the raw origin (scripts/memory-capture.sh:48-68). The key is created automatically by age-keygen on the first private capture (memory-capture.sh:69-81), so there is no setup step. A private capture does need an origin remote (memory-capture.sh:56-57), and the row omits this. scenario: a user hashes their literal HTTPS origin to provision the key; capture then looks for another filename and generates a second identity. on main: n/a. The no-plaintext claim holds: on failure the script refuses and writes nothing (memory-capture.sh:118-126).\n4. consider (self, accuracy): INSTALL.md `systemd-run` row. \"`wake` answers NOOP\" is too broad. Probe with no systemd-run on PATH: `can wake.arm` prints NOOP and exits 1, but `can wake.send` prints YES and exits 0. When systemd-run exists but the user manager is unusable, arm returns 2 (FAILED), not NOOP (scripts/runtime_wake.py:85, 169-172).\n5. consider (accuracy): INSTALL.md says make \"runs Python through `uv run --frozen`\". The Makefile instead uses the ambient interpreter when VIRTUAL_ENV is set or uv is missing (Makefile:8).\n6. consider (accuracy, self): \"check-agnostic.sh keeps vendor names out of skills and rules\" overstates what the script does. Its gh/github patterns apply only to skills/; rules/ gets only the CLAUDE_CODE_ and Skill( patterns (scripts/check-agnostic.sh:19-41).\nThese claims hold: the runtime.py backends, markers and exits; the forge backends with notes stores; routes.json launch_doors read by gaze_seat.py; Python >=3.11; the runtime floors in pilot-support.json checked by `idh check harness`; act+podman for local-ci; Zotero on 127.0.0.1:23119; the Pi wake inbox extension (ticket 1316 still open); tickets/erg as an ELF x86-64 binary; trackers 1309 and 1317.\nTargeted tests: selected: none; fallback: none; result: skipped (no source or test file changed).\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 3m54s\ntelemetry: wall=234s agents=1 tokens=unread cost~=$unread\nseat: self \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: accuracy \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 status: ran\n"}

